--   The bit loop.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSweep2`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.bits_sp (s : IState HS) (F : Fin HS → List ℤ) (z sv : List ℤ) (v : Fin 19 → List ℤ)
--       (bs : List ℤ) (B : ℕ) (hB : 1 ≤ B) (h01 : ∀ b ∈ bs, b = 0 ∨ b = 1)
--       (hd : v 3 = [(bs.length : ℤ)]) (hdB : zsz (bs.length : ℤ) ≤ B) (hbB : bs.length + 1 ≤ B)
--       (h4 : v 4 = [0]) (h12 : v 12 = []) (h16 : v 16 = []) :
--       Sp (.rep (σ 16) (.reg (σ 3)) (bitB σ dS)) (encK s (SS σ dS F z (bs ++ sv) v))
--         (encK s (SS σ dS F z sv (update (update v 12 bs.reverse) 4 [bs.sum])))
--         ((1 + 1) * 2000 * (B + 2) + bs.length * (20000 * (B + 2) + 8000 * (B + 2) + 30) + 32)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, B6 §2: reading the line descriptor
--
--   `hdrA σ dS` (on `dS = descLine6 = p :: α :: h :: d :: (bits ++ svals)`): pop `p, α, h, d` into
--   `σ 0..3`, move the `d` bits onto `σ 12` while counting the ones in `σ 4`, move them on to `σ 13`
--   (in order), then `σ 5 := T = 2^{h d + #ones}`, `σ 6 := 1` (`pre`), `σ 8 := 0` (`k`).
